+# The engine (B-109c) commits `saved` BETWEEN this playbook and home_wipe.yml, so capture and wipe
+# are separate playbooks. Order of the end-of-slot save: revoke -> capture (this) -> apps cleanup
+# (cleanup.yml) -> gated wipe (home_wipe.yml) -> verify_clean.yml.
+#
+# S never exists here: only S's PUBLIC recipient comes in. The script prints no path or file
+# name; its JSON (status, reason, raw_bytes, age_bytes, age_sha256) goes to daolab_output_file
+# for the runner. A refused capture leaves the home untouched and fails this playbook with
+# "capture refused: <reason>" (a fixed code); the engine then keeps the home and quarantines.
+#
+# Extra vars: reservation_id, setup + what play 0 reads (tasks/resolve.yml),
+#   daolab_snapshot_recipient   age1... (S's public recipient)
+#   daolab_snapshot_public_id   32 lowercase hex (the snapshot row's public_id)
+#   daolab_snapshot_cap_bytes   the raw tar cap (E-8, 512 MiB by default)
+#   daolab_snapshot_fetch_to    the controller path, <root>/u<uid>/.incoming/<public_id>.age.part
+#   daolab_output_file          where the report goes (the runner)
+# For tests only: daolab_dpu_root (a prefix for /home, /etc/skel, /var/lib/daolab) and
+# daolab_age_root (a prefix for /usr/local/bin, as tasks/install_age.yml).
